  "summary": "This prospective observational cohort study evaluates changes in high-frequency skin ultrasound findings in patients with cutaneous leishmaniasis receiving routine clinical treatment at the University Hospital of Brasilia, Brazil. The primary outcome is clinical cure assessed three months after completion of treatment. Ultrasonography will characterize dermal and hypodermal thickness, echogenicity and color Doppler vascular signals over repeated examinations. Associations of baseline clinical, histopathological, and ultrasound findings with healing will be investigated. Participants will be followed for 12 months from treatment initiation to evaluate their clinical course, including relapse.",
  "title": "High-Frequency Ultrasound Monitoring of Cutaneous Leishmaniasis During Treatment"
}

